-- title:
--   Extra levels match along i iff e_γ stabilises K
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $r$ and $\bar r$ are distinct primes (`hrr`) and $N$ is a squarefree natural number divisible by neither of them (`hrN`, `hrbarN`, `hN`).
--
--   **Coefficients** (`hdvr`–`hvdet`). $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi$ an irreducible element of $\mathcal O$, $\mathcal O$ is $\pi$-adically complete, $\#(\mathcal O/\pi)=r$ and $(r)=(\pi)$; $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$. The ring `Onr` is a characteristic-zero domain and $\mathcal O$-algebra carrying an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$; it is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every element of `Onr` satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree over `Onr` has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod{\pi}$ (`hFr`). Further, `vdet` is a homomorphism from $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ to $\mathbb Z$ written multiplicatively, which by `hvdet` assigns $n$ to $g$ exactly when $\det g=u\,\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Indefinite quaternion side and moduli** (`hB`–`harbar`). The hypothesis `hB` says that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ has $0<a$ or $0<b$ and is ramified at exactly the finite places above $r$ and $\bar r$; $\Lambda$ is a maximal order in it (`hΛ`). The scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point assignment `pt` is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure (`h𝒳`: invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change, bijectivity on geometric points, and the universal property). An integer $n\ge 3$ is given, prime to $r$, to $\bar r$ and to $N$ (`hn`, `hrn`, `hrbarn`, `hnN`), together with a fine moduli space $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ for such curves with full level-$n$ structure (`hM`) and a group $G$ acting on $M$ by automorphisms $\rho$ with labels $\chi:G\to\Lambda$ realising the level twists (`hρ`, whose clauses — action over the base, realisation of twists, multiplicativity and bijectivity of $\chi$ modulo $n$ — are summarised here). The morphism $p:M\to\mathcal X$ lies over the base (`hp`), is invariant under the $G$-action (`hρp`) and forgets the full level structure on points (`hp_pt`). For each prime $\ell$ distinct from $r,\bar r$, $\mathcal Y_\ell$ is a coarse moduli space for curves with an additional level-$\ell$ subgroup (`h𝒴`) and $d_0,d_1:\mathcal Y_\ell\to\mathcal X$ are the two degeneracy morphisms over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`), $d_0$ forgetting the $\ell$-structure (`hd₀`) and $d_1$ sending it to the quotient isogeny target (`hd₁`). Finally $a_r,a_{\bar r}:\mathcal X\to\mathcal X$ are morphisms over the base inducing the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`harf`, `harbarf`, `har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite quaternion side** (`hdef`–`hwbar`). The algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ has $a_1,b_1<0$ and is ramified exactly at the place above $\bar r$ (`hdef`); $\Lambda_1$ is a maximal order, $R_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$ contained in $\Lambda_1$ (`hΛ₁`, `hR₁`, `hRΛ₁`), $n_1$ an idele in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ (`hn₁`) such that $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`), and $\iota_0$ an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map into $M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`); $v$ is the place of $\mathbb Q$ above $r$ (`hv`). The subgroup $\Gamma^{t}$ consists of the units integral away from $v$ (`hΓt`: it equals [`CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.awayUnits R₁ v`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_CosetGraphAtPrime.html#L37)). For each prime $\ell\ne r,\bar r$ elements $s_\ell$ and $s^{f}_\ell$ are given with (`hs`): the component of $s^f_\ell$ at each place not above $r$ is $s_\ell\otimes 1$, its component above $r$ is $1$, the product of the diagonal idele of the scalar $\ell$ with $(s^f_\ell)^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` if $\ell\mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$; the groups $\Gamma^t_\ell$ are the intersections $\Gamma^t\cap s_\ell\Gamma^t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`). The element $\bar w$ has reduced norm $\bar r$ and normalises $\Gamma^t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **Special fibre and its endomorphisms** (`hΛℤ`–`hE5e`). All rational integers lie in $\Lambda$ (`hΛℤ`), and `coord` embeds $\Lambda$ into a pair of Witt-coordinate rings compatibly with the twisted multiplication, densely and with the prescribed trace (`hcoord`). Over the residue ring $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi$ there are: a fake elliptic curve $A_0$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of dimension $2$ along the unit section of $A_0$, and families $e,e':\Gamma^t\to\operatorname{End}(A_0)$ over the base (`he`) with degrees `deg`, such that $A_0$ is a formal module via `coord`, $X_0$, $\theta_0$ (`hA₀`). The hypotheses on these are: `hE1` ($e_\gamma,e'_\gamma$ form an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ and $e_\gamma$ preserves the level-$N$ structure), `hE1mul` (multiplicativity of $\gamma\mapsto e_\gamma$ up to powers of $r$), `hE1sc` (a rational integral scalar $\gamma=c$ gives multiplication by $c$ up to powers of $r$), `hE1'` (conversely, if $e_\gamma$ becomes a positive integral multiplication after a power of $r$ then $\gamma$ is a rational scalar), `hE2` (for every injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and $\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $\gamma$ has a centralising endomorphism $\varepsilon$ inducing $e_\gamma$ on formal coordinates with $E_0\varepsilon=r^{k_\gamma}\,g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$), `hE3` (each full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ admits a labelling $\mathrm{lab}:\Gamma^t\to\Lambda$ describing the action of $e_\gamma$ on $P_0$, multiplicative and scalar-compatible modulo $n$) and `hE4` (over an algebraically closed field over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi$, every $r$-power-degree, level-preserving isogeny pair of a pullback of $A_0$ comes from some $e_\gamma$ up to powers of $r$). Moreover an order $R_2\le R_1$ with $r$-power denominators (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`, `hR₂r`) acts by $\hat e$ on $A_0$ over the base (`hê`), additively, $\Lambda$-equivariantly and preserving the level (`hE5a`), unitally and multiplicatively, with integers acting as multiplications (`hE5b1`, `hE5b2`, `hE5b3`), with $\hat e(\bar x)\hat e(x)$ multiplication by $\mathrm{nrd}(x)$ (`hE5c`), compatibly with $e_\gamma$ on $r^k\gamma$ (`hE5d`), and `hE5e` gives one $g$ realising simultaneously the matrix descriptions of both the $\Gamma^t$- and the $R_2$-endomorphisms.
--
--   **Drinfeld moduli side** (`ι`–`hPiexD`). $\iota$ is a ring map from the Witt coordinates to `Onr`, $\Phi$ a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over `Onr`$/(r)$ which is special relative to $\iota$ (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`), `MD` a moduli package over `Onr` satisfying the Zariski sheaf axiom (`hMD`), and $\eta$ assigns to every rigidified object over a ring in which $r$ is nilpotent a point of `MD`, with (`hη`, three clauses): $\eta$ separates admissible rigidified objects exactly up to isomorphism, is compatible with base change, and is locally surjective along a Zariski cover by localisations. The map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and $\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ is injective and its image is squeezed between $r^{m}M_2(\mathcal O)$ and $r^{-m}M_2(\mathcal O)$ for some $m$ (`hE₀`). The family `eD` compares the functor of points of `MD` over $\mathcal O$ with the product of the functor corepresented by `Onr` and Drinfeld's functor $\Omega$ of Deligne data: it is natural (`hnatD`), bijective on every noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra in which $\pi$ is nilpotent (`hbijD`), has first coordinate the structural map $\psi$ (`hfstD`), turns the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action `ModuliPackage.G.IsActBy` into the twisted action `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` (`hGLD`), sends $\pi$-translates to the Frobenius twist of the $\psi$-leg with unchanged Deligne datum (`hPiD`), and $\pi$-translates always exist (`hPiexD`). In addition $\kappa$ is a ring map $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi\to O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps (`hκ`), and $\beta_0$ is an isogeny from $\Phi$ to $X_0$ reduced along $\kappa$, of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`). A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$ is fixed. The Atkin–Lehner datum at $\bar r$ on the special fibre consists of $A_{0w}$, morphisms $a_w,a_w'$ exhibiting it as the quotient at $\bar r$ (`hALw`), and $b_w,b_w'$ forming an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ which preserves the level (`hBSw`, `hBSwlev`), with `hJOINTw` providing one $g$ realising both the matrix description of the $\Gamma^t$-endomorphisms and a matrix description of $a_w$ followed by $b_w$ by $\bar w$.
--
--   **The comparison map and the one-leg axioms** (`Ξ`–`hC3`). For every noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and every $\psi:O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$, $\Xi$ sends a pair consisting of a fake elliptic curve over $B$ together with a rigidification relative to $A_0$ and $\psi$ to a point of the formal moduli functor, and satisfies: `hΞleg` (over $B$ with only trivial idempotents the $\psi$-leg of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist $\mathrm{Fr}^{k}$ of $\psi$), `hΞnat` (compatibility with pullbacks of rigidified curves), `hΞiso` (invariance under an isomorphism of the underlying curves together with comparison data on the rigidifications matching the isogenies after multiplication by powers of $r$), and `hΞdef` (over connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent, for any formal module structure $(X,\theta)$ on the curve there are $j\le 1$ and an admissible rigidified object $t$ with $t.X=X$ transporting $\theta_0,\kappa,\beta_0$ to $\theta$ in $j$ steps, such that $\Xi$ equals the point built from $\mathrm{Fr}^{-j}\psi$ and $\eta\,t$). A fixed $g_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ is given, and: `heqΓ` (translating a rigidification by $e_\gamma$ corresponds to the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$ for some $c\in\mathbb Z$), `heqW` (an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$, with comparison data lifting $a_w$ followed by $b_w$, corresponds to the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\bar w)g_0^{-1}$). The one-leg axioms are `hK1` (every $(\psi,P)$ over a connected $B$ is realised by a rigidified curve whose $\Xi$-leg is the twist $\mathrm{Fr}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0)}\psi$ and whose $g_0^{-1}$-twisted image under `eD` is $(\psi,P)$), `hK2` (two such realisations are isomorphic, with comparison data on the rigidifications), `hK3` (the realisations are compatible with base change along $\varphi:B\to B'$) and `hK4` (they lift along a surjection with square-zero kernel, the twisted-action condition being unaffected). The transported full level-$n$ structure exists (`hC0e`) and its underlying point is unique (`hC0u`). The family $\Theta_f$ sends a triple consisting of $\psi$, a Deligne datum $P$ and an element of $G$ to a $B$-point of $M$ over the base, naturally (`hnat`), with $\rho_h$ carrying $\Theta_f(x,gh)$ to $\Theta_f(x,g)$ (`hG`), and on one-leg data with transported level $P_n$ it agrees with the fine moduli point of $(E,P_n)$ (`hC2`) and, after composing with $p$, with the coarse moduli point of $E$ (`hC2c`). Finally $\theta^{t}:\Gamma^{t}\to G$ is a homomorphism and `hC3` is the Hecke-translation axiom: given a one-leg datum $(\psi,P)$ for $(E,\varrho)$ over a connected $B$ and $\gamma\in\Gamma^{t}$ with $(\psi,P)$ carried to $(\psi',P')$ by the $\iota_0(\gamma)$-twisted action, there is a rigidification $\varrho'$ of the same $E$ with the one-leg property for $(\psi',P')$, whose transported level-$n$ structure is the $\chi(\theta^{t}\gamma)$-translate of that of $\varrho$, and such that for every prime $\ell\ne r$ invertible in $B$ and every level-$\ell$ extra structure on $A_0$ stabilised by $e_\gamma$, any two extra structures on $E$ transported from it through $\varrho$ and through $\varrho'$ have the same points.
--
--   **The situation at an algebraically closed point.** Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent in it (`hk`), let $\psi:O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to k$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra map and $P,P'$ two Deligne data over $k$. Let $E,E'$ be fake elliptic curves over $k$ with rigidifications $\varrho,\varrho'$ relative to the twisted leg $\mathrm{Fr}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0)}\psi$, such that the $\Xi$-legs of $(E,\varrho)$ and $(E',\varrho')$ equal that twist (`hΞψ`, `hΞψ'`) and the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted action carries their images under `eD` to $(\psi,P)$, respectively $(\psi,P')$ (`hev`, `hev'`). Let $i:E.A\cong E'.A$ be an isomorphism over $k$ (`hi`) compatible with the group laws, the $\Lambda$-actions and the level-$N$ structures (`hvia`). Let $\gamma\in\Gamma^{t}$ (`hγ`), and let $\varrho''$ be a third rigidification of the same $E$ whose $\Xi$-leg is correct and whose `eD`-image is carried to $(\psi,P')$ (`hev''`), where $(\psi,P)$ is carried to $(\psi,P')$ by the $\iota_0(\gamma)$-twisted action (`htw`). Two further hypotheses concern the pair $(\varrho,\varrho'')$: `hell` asserts that for every prime $\ell\ne r$ invertible in $k$ and every level-$\ell$ extra structure $\mathcal K$ on $A_0$ stabilised by $e_{\gamma}$, any extra structures $C$ and $C'$ on $E$ transported from $\mathcal K$ through $\varrho$ and through $\varrho''$ respectively have the same points; `hdet` asserts the converse implication, namely that if $C$ and $C''$, transported from $\mathcal K$ through $\varrho$ and through $\varrho''$, have the same points, then $e_{\gamma}$ maps $\mathcal K$ into itself. Finally `hcorr` provides comparison data between $\varrho''$ and $\varrho'$ along $i$: morphisms $i_b$ and $u_A$ compatible with $g_b$, $g_A$ and the structural morphisms, with $u_A$ exhibiting $\varrho'.A_b$ as a pullback of $\varrho''.A_b$ along the identity, and natural numbers $i_1,j_1$ for which $i_b$ followed by $\varrho'.\varphi$, $u_A$ and multiplication by $r^{i_1}$ equals $\varrho''.\varphi$ followed by multiplication by $r^{j_1}$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every prime $\ell$ with $\ell\ne r$ and $\ell$ invertible in $k$, every level-$\ell$ extra structure $\mathcal K$ on $A_0$ (its Lean binder reuses the name `K₀`), every level-$\ell$ extra structure $C$ on $E$ and every level-$\ell$ extra structure $C'$ on $E'$, assume
--
--   (i) $C$ is transported from $\mathcal K$ through $\varrho$: for every scheme $T$, every $t':T\to\operatorname{Spec}(k/(\pi))$ and every $T$-point $R$ of $\varrho.E_b$ over $t'$, if $R$ followed by $\varrho.g_b$ factors through $C.\mathrm{levK}$, then $R$ followed by $\varrho.\varphi$ and then by $\varrho.g_A$ factors through $\mathcal K.\mathrm{levK}$; and
--
--   (ii) the same for $C'$ through $\varrho'$: for every $T$, every $t':T\to\operatorname{Spec}(k/(\pi))$ and every $T$-point $R$ of $\varrho'.E_b$ over $t'$, if $R$ followed by $\varrho'.g_b$ factors through $C'.\mathrm{levK}$, then $R$ followed by $\varrho'.\varphi$ and then by $\varrho'.g_A$ factors through $\mathcal K.\mathrm{levK}$.
--
--   Then the following two statements are equivalent:
--
--   (a) for every scheme $T$, every $t:T\to\operatorname{Spec}k$ and every $T$-point $R$ of $E$ over $t$: $R$ factors through $C.\mathrm{levK}$ if and only if $R$ followed by $i$ factors through $C'.\mathrm{levK}$;
--
--   (b) $e_{\gamma}$ maps $\mathcal K$ into itself: for every scheme $T$, every $t:T\to\operatorname{Spec}(O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi)$ and every $T$-point $R$ of $A_0$ over $t$, if $R$ factors through $\mathcal K.\mathrm{levK}$ then $R$ followed by $e_{\gamma}$ factors through $\mathcal K.\mathrm{levK}$.
--
--   This is the extra-level-$\ell$ clause of the one-leg fibre computation in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of the Shimura curve attached to the indefinite quaternion algebra ramified at $r$ and $\bar r$: it identifies, for an isomorphism $i$ between two fake elliptic curves occurring in the same fibre of the comparison map $\Xi$, the condition that level-$\ell$ subgroup schemes transported from a base subgroup $\mathcal K$ on the special fibre correspond under $i$ with the condition that the endomorphism $e_\gamma$ attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma^{t}$ stabilises $\mathcal K$. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.Rigidification.exists_mem_isPullback_of_isoVia_levelHom_of_translate_of_isAlgClosed_heightNormalised_eq_of_oneLeg_levelHomLaw`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.Rigidification.exists_mem_isPullback_of_isoVia_levelHom_of_translate_of_isAlgClosed_heightNormalised_eq_of_oneLeg_levelHomLaw), where the Hecke correspondences on the tower of extra-level moduli spaces are matched with the $p$-adic uniformisation.
